{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)arctan({x}^{3}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-19067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the product rule, using the formula for the derivative of $arctanx$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =arctan({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1))+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arctan({x}^{3})) \\\\  & =arctan({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+({x}^{3})^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =arctan({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+({x}^{3})^{2}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2xarctan({x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}{1+{x}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-19067" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fac208126a61a4a65a1120bd5a5b8c90472c02d963c1e82c7743f2d7fce2c84"} {"question" "q-19067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-19067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2xarctan({x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}{1+{x}^{6}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2xarctan({x}^{3})}{{x}^{6}+1}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}{1+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{6}}"] ["math" "\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{6}}"] ["math" "\\frac{arctan({x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}{1+{x}^{6}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-19067" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2xarctan({x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+1}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+1)}{1+{x}^{6}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the slope of the tangent line to the curve $f(x)=6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{x}^{2}-2x)$ at $x=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3{x}^{2}-2x)] \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+(3{x}^{2}-2x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1+9{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot (6x-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{36x-12}{9{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve $y=f(x)$ at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{36(1)-12}{9({1}^{4})-12({1}^{3})+4({1}^{2})+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fac208126a61a4a65a1120bd5a5b8c90472c02d963c1e82c7743f2d7fce2c84"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "24"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-31823" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the product rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)) & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fac208126a61a4a65a1120bd5a5b8c90472c02d963c1e82c7743f2d7fce2c84"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5-x)"] ["math" "\\frac{(5-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{(5-x)}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{(5-x)}^{2}}}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(5-x)"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-73510" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{(5-x)}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(5-x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7{x}^{4}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of arctangent is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(7{x}^{4})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+{(7{x}^{4})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+49{x}^{8}}\\cdot 28{x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{28{x}^{3}}{49{x}^{8}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fac208126a61a4a65a1120bd5a5b8c90472c02d963c1e82c7743f2d7fce2c84"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{28{x}^{3}}{49{x}^{4}+1}"] ["math" "-\\frac{28{x}^{3}}{7{x}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{28{x}^{3}}{49{x}^{8}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{28{x}^{4}}{7{x}^{8}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{49{x}^{8}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-110627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{28{x}^{3}}{49{x}^{8}+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-343215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve $y=2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+x)$ at $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-343215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1+x)] \\\\  & =2(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(1+x)^{2}}})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-(1+2x+{x}^{2})}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2x-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the curve at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{-2(-1)-(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/state.json" "file_sha256" "bb51122f879df2415fead8002aa994bede79091c89243aeb15be3ecea5e7fcbe"} {"question" "q-343215" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13994894/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fac208126a61a4a65a1120bd5a5b8c90472c02d963c1e82c7743f2d7fce2c84"} {"question" "q-3